            <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">
                Your organisation may not need to comply with the new regulations
            </h1>
            <p class="govuk-body">
                Based on your answers, your heat network does not fall within scope of the new HNTAS technical requirements.
            </p>
            <p class="govuk-body">However, you may still need to comply with Ofgem's heat network regulations for existing networks.</p>

            <p class="govuk-body">
                Review <a class="govuk-link" target="_blank" href="https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ofgem.gov.uk%2Fenergy-regulation%2Flow-carbon%2Fheat-networks&data=05%7C02%7CPradeep.Kirubagaran%40energysecurity.gov.uk%7Cf5f629ad5f604b481e4708de8b599119%7Ccbac700502c143ebb497e6492d1b2dd8%7C0%7C0%7C639101413967322253%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=FAephFFl7FGjzXKxUJpMtSAe%2BpTPGc%2BJbQW6fTdrPRE%3D&reserved=0">Ofgem guidance (opens in new tab)</a> to check whether you need to register your heat network or apply for authorisation.
            </p>

        </div>
